{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Algebraic SI Derived Units.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Algebraic SI Derived Units.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"algebraic si derived units algebraic si derived units","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Algebraic SI Derived Units.md","fileName":"Algebraic SI Derived Units.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Algebraic SI Derived Units","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision","Seven SI Base Units","Dimensional Homogeneity in Equations","dimensionalanalysisforunitconversionusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Algebraic SI Derived Units.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Algebraic SI Derived Units.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"algebraic si derived units algebraic si derived units","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Algebraic SI Derived Units.md","fileName":"Algebraic SI Derived Units.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Algebraic SI Derived Units","heading":"Algebraic SI Derived Units","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A derived SI unit is built by multiplying or dividing base units. The book's Table 2-2 writes force as the newton, $\\mathrm{N}=\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-2}}$, and pressure as the pascal, $\\mathrm{Pa}=\\mathrm{kg\\,m^{-1}\\,s^{-2}}$. Special names make frequently used combinations shorter without changing their dimensional structure. Radian and steradian are listed with a unit expression of one because matching lengths or areas cancel. See [[Seven SI Base Units]] and [[Dimensional Homogeneity in Equations]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Unit Algebra and Measurement Precision","Seven SI Base Units","Dimensional Homogeneity in Equations","di